<title>BANGLADESH: Chittagong port handles 15,125 tonnes of cargo.</title>
<headline>Chittagong port handles 15,125 tonnes of cargo.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh's main Chittagong port handled 15,125 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours ending at 1.00 p.m. (0700 GMT) on Wednesday compared with 14,486 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday, port officials said.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					Wednesday	    Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo		   1,592		   288</p>
<p>    Import cargo		  13,533		  14,198</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Chittagong port:</p>
<p>    Commodity		 Tonnes     Ship		 Berthing</p>
<p>    Phosphate		 13,000     Da Cheng	   20/11</p>
<p>    High Speed Diesel     20,647     Canopus	    22/11</p>
<p>    Superior Kerosene     19,870     Entalina	   22/11</p>
<p>    Wheat		     25,000     Great Cheer	23/11</p>
<p>    Cement		    30,000     Tian Sheng No.8  25/11</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
